2. Introduction
Software maintenance is the process of modifying and updating software after its delivery to correct errors, improve performance, and adapt to changing requirements.

Software reengineering is the process of analyzing and modifying an existing software system to improve its structure, quality, and performance without completely developing a new system.

AI-assisted software engineering uses Artificial Intelligence tools to automate coding, testing, debugging, and software quality improvement.

In this case study, a college wants to modernize its existing Student Management System using software maintenance, reengineering, and AI tools.
3. Problem Analysis
The existing Student Management System faces several problems:
1. Slow Performance: The system takes more time to load student records and generate reports.
2. Outdated Features: Some features do not meet current college requirements.
3. Frequent Errors: The system produces errors during data entry and processing.
4. Poor User Experience: The interface is difficult for students and staff to use.
5. Maintenance Difficulties: Old code makes it difficult to modify and update the system.
These problems reduce system efficiency and affect the daily activities of the college.
4. Proposed Solution
The college can improve the existing system using the following software engineering techniques.
A. Software Maintenance
Software maintenance helps improve the existing system after deployment.

Suitable types of software maintenance:

1. Corrective Maintenance: Fixes errors and bugs in the existing system.
- Example: Correcting errors in student attendance records.
2. Adaptive Maintenance: Modifies software to work with new technologies or environments.
- Example: Updating the system to support new operating systems and databases.
3. Perfective Maintenance: Improves performance and adds new features.
- Example: Adding online fee payment and attendance tracking.
4. Preventive Maintenance: Reduces future problems by improving code quality.
- Example: Removing unnecessary code and improving system security.
B. Software Reengineering
Software reengineering improves an existing software system by analyzing and restructuring it.

Steps involved in software reengineering:
1. Inventory Analysis: Identify existing software components and their problems.
2. Document Restructuring: Update outdated system documentation.
3. Reverse Engineering: Study the existing system to understand its design and functionality.
4. Code Restructuring: Improve the existing code without changing its main functionality.
5. Data Restructuring: Organize and improve the database structure.
6. Forward Engineering: Develop and implement the modernized system.
Example: The college can convert its old Student Management System into a modern web-based application with an improved database and user interface.
C. Applications of AI in Software Engineering
AI tools can help improve software development and maintenance.

1. AI-Based Bug Detection and Debugging
- AI tools identify errors in program code.
- Suggest possible solutions to developers.
- Reduce debugging time.
- Improve software quality.
Example: GitHub Copilot can assist developers in understanding and improving code.

2. AI-Based Automated Software Testing
- AI helps generate test cases automatically.
- Identifies defects during software testing.
- Checks system performance.
- Reduces manual testing effort.
Example: AI-assisted testing tools can test student registration, login, and fee payment functions.
5. Expected Improvements
The modernization process provides the following three major improvements:
1. Improved Performance: The system becomes faster and processes student information efficiently.
2. Better Reliability: Bug fixing and automated testing reduce errors and improve software quality.
3. Enhanced Functionality: New features such as online fee payment, attendance tracking, and automated report generation improve user experience.
